Z||000000||fierocd||06-04-2001||09:01 PM||||My friends and I came up with an idea and we were wondering if anyone has any idea if this would do anything.  I have an extra blower for the trunk, so we were wondering what difference it would make if we somehow tapped that into the air inlet hose before the plenum and hooked it up to a toggle switch.  We are figuring this would be something like an all time ram-air.  Any ideas on if this would do anything???||||reg||3
Z||000001||PBJ||06-04-2001||09:48 PM||||If you wired it up properly you could maybe help charge the battery, cause the air sucked into an engine is far more than any electric fan can produce. It would take more electricity to run a fan big enough than the power it would produce.  SO what I am saying is the air intake from the motor would turn the fan blade faster than the mtr could.  My opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||06-04-2001||11:29 PM||||Hey CD!<BR>Depends on the flow rate and fan style as to it working...<BR>If it produces more flow than the engine, then the style of fan determines if it will develope positive pressure differential in an amount usefull to produce more power...<BR>All fancy speak for a simple blower...<BR>Far easier to get a Paxton supercharger and plumb it in...<BR>At least you know it works!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
